* Name: "mergeGraphs",
* Signature: "private void mergeGraphs(final List<File> sources, final File target) throws IOException"
* Purpose: "The `mergeGraphs` method is designed to aggregate data from multiple RRD (Round Robin Database) files, listed in `sources`, into a single target RRD file. The method initially copies the first source file to the target location and uses it as the base for merging data from subsequent source files. Conditional logic adjusts the merging behavior for files that reflect percentage values, such as those related to CPU and system errors, by applying a coefficient that averages the data if the last source file is reached. Each source RRD database is opened, merged into the base (target), and then closed to free resources. If any errors occur, such as an `RrdException`, the method logs the error and deletes the target file to prevent incomplete or inconsistent aggregation results."
* Method declaration: 

"""
1. private void mergeGraphs(final List<File> sources, final File target) throws IOException {
2.     try {
3.         RrdDb mergedRrdDb = null;
4.         Double coeff = null;
5.         final String name = target.getName();
6.         final boolean percentageValues = "cpu.rrd".equals(name) || "gc.rrd".equals(name) || "systemCpuLoad.rrd".equals(name) || name.endsWith("SystemErrors.rrd");
7.         final File lastSource = sources.get(sources.size() - 1);
8.         for (final File source : sources) {
9.             if (mergedRrdDb == null) {
10.                 InputOutput.copyFile(source, target);
11.                 mergedRrdDb = new RrdDb(target.getPath());
12.             } else {
13.                 if (percentageValues && source.equals(lastSource)) {
14.                     coeff = 1d / sources.size();
15.                 }
16.                 final RrdDb sourceRrdDb = new RrdDb(source.getPath());
17.                 try {
18.                     mergeRrdDbs(sourceRrdDb, mergedRrdDb, coeff);
19.                 } finally {
20.                     sourceRrdDb.close();
21.                 }
22.             }
23.         }
24.         mergedRrdDb.close();
25.     } catch (final RrdException e) {
26.         log(e.toString());
27.         InputOutput.deleteFile(target);
